Z||000000||Capt Fiero||11-23-2001||12:04 AM||||I am going to need to pass a very strict emmisions test, the local test has changed a bit and no longer includes visual inspection of engine.  Here is the short of it.  2.8 V6, 1985.  Big Cam, (.426 lift, 280adv duration) 19# injectors, Complete MSD Ignition.) NO EGR SYSTEM AT ALL.  I plan to put a catyl. converter on it. But they do test for NOX.  What are some good things to reduce emmisions.  My big concern is dropping the cylnder temps down to an average level in hops of getting the NOX readings down.  I have heard from some people that with my motor I might be best off using the cheapest gas possibe and others say that I should use the highest grade I can get plus add some methylhydrate.  I really dont want to add or change any hard parts of the car execpt the catyl converter.  Does anyone have any sugestions. The test is not for another month, but at 24$ per test I dont really want to have to test and retest more than once.<P>David<BR>85GT<P>------------------<BR>David<BR>85GT<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://photos.onebigvillage.com/pubimage.asp?id_=32415"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||11-23-2001||12:30 AM||||Hey David!<BR>Depending on what and when you did your mods, you should have no worries...<BR>If you did an entire rebuild, and it wasn't over a couple of years ago, then adding the cat converter should be plenty...<BR>Also, most tests factor in the age of the vehicle, so they are testing a 16 year old car...<BR>Just be sure the car is fully warmed up before the test so the cat is hot enough to work!<BR>If by chance you fail the test (unlikely), be sure to get the printout of the test to pinpoint the trouble area...<BR>And please let us know how it goes!<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierobruiser||11-23-2001||01:21 AM||||I passed PA emmissions tests in the past with high miles cars other than Fieros that I have known should have failed the test by filling the tank with the highest octane available and adding two cans of dry gas. I don't know if thats methylhydrate or not. That seemed to get good readings from the test machine. Good luck.<P>------------------<BR>Notchbacks Rule<BR>85GT(show car)<BR>88Coupe (daily driver)<BR>84 Coupe(project car)||||reg||1
